  "title": "Methane Gas - Specific Heat vs. Temperature",
  "description": "Calculate the specific heat (Cp) of Methane Gas (CH4) at temperatures ranging from 200 to 1100 K. Isobaric specific heat (Cp) is used for substances in constant pressure systems. The specific heat varies with temperature and should be corrected for accurate calculations in heated or cooled systems.",
